// The application icon: the FreeWili orca, copied byte-for-byte from fwcom's
// product.ico (freewilimain/testprojects/fwcom/product.ico) so this app and
// fwcom present the same product to the user rather than two near-identical
// drawings that drift apart.
//
// This one line is the whole of the icon wiring -- there is deliberately no
// runtime SDL_SetWindowIcon() call to go with it. SDL3 enumerates RT_GROUP_ICON
// and adopts the FIRST icon in the executable as the window class icon
// ("Use the first icon as a default icon, like in the Explorer",
// SDL_RegisterApp in SDL_windowsevents.c), so linking this resource sets the
// title-bar, Alt-Tab, taskbar AND Explorer icons at once. Adding a second icon
// resource to this executable would make "the first one" ambiguous; keep it to
// this one.
//
// The numeric ID matters for that reason too: an unquoted identifier the RC
// compiler cannot resolve to a number becomes a NAMED resource, and named
// resources sort after numeric ones. 1 keeps this unambiguously first.
1 ICON "product.ico"
